      company_id: 'comp-google',
      company_name: 'Google',
      canonical_title: 'Staff Machine Learning Infrastructure Engineer (PyTorch / TPU)',
      title: 'Staff Machine Learning Infrastructure Engineer (PyTorch / TPU)',
      description_text: "### About Google DeepMind & AI Systems\nGoogle DeepMind is a world-leading team of scientists, engineers, and researchers committed to solving intelligence to advance science and benefit humanity. From breakthrough models like Gemini to AlphaFold, our AI systems push the boundaries of computational intelligence.\n\nThe **DeepMind Foundation Infrastructure** team builds the supercomputing orchestrators, distributed checkpointing engines, and high-performance communication fabrics required to train trillion-parameter foundation models across tens of thousands of TPU v5p and NVIDIA GPU accelerators.\n\n### The Role & Technical Scope\nAs a Staff Machine Learning Infrastructure Engineer, you will own the architectural design and scaling of large-scale distributed training orchestration tools using Go (Golang) and Python. You will eliminate communication bottlenecks in distributed collective operations (AllReduce, AllGather), optimize TPU slice allocation across Google Borg and Kubernetes clusters, and build self-healing infrastructure that automatically detects and replaces faulty accelerator nodes without aborting long-running training jobs.\n\n### Key Responsibilities:\n- Build high-scale distributed training orchestration tools and control-plane microservices using Go (Golang) and Python.\n- Scale multi-host TPU v5p, TPU v6, and GPU clusters, maximizing Model FLOPs Utilization (MFU) across large-scale pre-training runs.\n- Develop fault-tolerant checkpointing pipelines capable of writing terabyte-scale model states to distributed storage in under 10 seconds.\n- Design low-latency inter-accelerator networking layers utilizing ICI (Inter-Chip Interconnect) and Google Jupiter datacenter fabric.\n- Implement custom Kubernetes operators in Go for dynamic GPU/TPU slice provisioning, job preemption, and priority scheduling.\n- Partner with foundation model research scientists to profile training bottlenecks, kernel execution times, and memory saturation.\n- Lead incident triage and post-mortems for large-scale training cluster interruptions, driving automated hardware health diagnostics.\n- Champion engineering excellence, code review standards, and architectural blueprints across the DeepMind infrastructure organization.\n\n### Minimum Qualifications:\n- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or equivalent experience.\n- 7+ years of systems engineering experience developing backend infrastructure and cluster tooling in Go (Golang), C++, or Python.\n- Proven expertise in large-scale machine learning training infrastructure, GPU/TPU cluster orchestration, and high-performance networking.\n- Hands-on experience with PyTorch, JAX, or TensorFlow distributed execution (FSDP, Megatron-style tensor parallelism, pipeline parallelism).\n- Deep understanding of container runtimes, Kubernetes architecture, Linux kernel cgroups, and resource isolation.\n\n### Preferred Qualifications:\n- Experience operating clusters with 1,000+ accelerators and high-bandwidth interconnects (NCCL, RoCE, InfiniBand).\n- Author of published research or open-source libraries in distributed systems, high-performance computing (HPC), or LLM orchestration.\n- Expertise with low-level kernel tracing, eBPF, and network packet telemetry.\n\n### Total Rewards & Benefits:\n- **Base Salary Range:** $240,000 \u2013 $320,000 USD per year.\n- **Equity:** Substantial Google Stock Unit (GSU) grant with regular refreshers.\n- **Perks:** Comprehensive health insurance, onsite medical care, continuous learning budget, 401(k) matching, and flexible hybrid remote schedule.\n\n### Equal Employment Opportunity:\nGoogle DeepMind is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer.",
      description: "### About Google DeepMind & AI Systems\nGoogle DeepMind is a world-leading team of scientists, engineers, and researchers committed to solving intelligence to advance science and benefit humanity. From breakthrough models like Gemini to AlphaFold, our AI systems push the boundaries of computational intelligence.\n\nThe **DeepMind Foundation Infrastructure** team builds the supercomputing orchestrators, distributed checkpointing engines, and high-performance communication fabrics required to train trillion-parameter foundation models across tens of thousands of TPU v5p and NVIDIA GPU accelerators.\n\n### The Role & Technical Scope\nAs a Staff Machine Learning Infrastructure Engineer, you will own the architectural design and scaling of large-scale distributed training orchestration tools using Go (Golang) and Python. You will eliminate communication bottlenecks in distributed collective operations (AllReduce, AllGather), optimize TPU slice allocation across Google Borg and Kubernetes clusters, and build self-healing infrastructure that automatically detects and replaces faulty accelerator nodes without aborting long-running training jobs.\n\n### Key Responsibilities:\n- Build high-scale distributed training orchestration tools and control-plane microservices using Go (Golang) and Python.\n- Scale multi-host TPU v5p, TPU v6, and GPU clusters, maximizing Model FLOPs Utilization (MFU) across large-scale pre-training runs.\n- Develop fault-tolerant checkpointing pipelines capable of writing terabyte-scale model states to distributed storage in under 10 seconds.\n- Design low-latency inter-accelerator networking layers utilizing ICI (Inter-Chip Interconnect) and Google Jupiter datacenter fabric.\n- Implement custom Kubernetes operators in Go for dynamic GPU/TPU slice provisioning, job preemption, and priority scheduling.\n- Partner with foundation model research scientists to profile training bottlenecks, kernel execution times, and memory saturation.\n- Lead incident triage and post-mortems for large-scale training cluster interruptions, driving automated hardware health diagnostics.\n- Champion engineering excellence, code review standards, and architectural blueprints across the DeepMind infrastructure organization.\n\n### Minimum Qualifications:\n- Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or equivalent experience.\n- 7+ years of systems engineering experience developing backend infrastructure and cluster tooling in Go (Golang), C++, or Python.\n- Proven expertise in large-scale machine learning training infrastructure, GPU/TPU cluster orchestration, and high-performance networking.\n- Hands-on experience with PyTorch, JAX, or TensorFlow distributed execution (FSDP, Megatron-style tensor parallelism, pipeline parallelism).\n- Deep understanding of container runtimes, Kubernetes architecture, Linux kernel cgroups, and resource isolation.\n\n### Preferred Qualifications:\n- Experience operating clusters with 1,000+ accelerators and high-bandwidth interconnects (NCCL, RoCE, InfiniBand).\n- Author of published research or open-source libraries in distributed systems, high-performance computing (HPC), or LLM orchestration.\n- Expertise with low-level kernel tracing, eBPF, and network packet telemetry.\n\n### Total Rewards & Benefits:\n- **Base Salary Range:** $240,000 \u2013 $320,000 USD per year.\n- **Equity:** Substantial Google Stock Unit (GSU) grant with regular refreshers.\n- **Perks:** Comprehensive health insurance, onsite medical care, continuous learning budget, 401(k) matching, and flexible hybrid remote schedule.\n\n### Equal Employment Opportunity:\nGoogle DeepMind is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer.",
