      canonical_title: 'Senior Software Development Engineer, AWS Core Distributed Storage (Go / Rust)',
      title: 'Senior Software Development Engineer, AWS Core Distributed Storage (Go / Rust)',
      description_text: "### About Amazon Web Services (AWS) Storage\nAmazon Web Services (AWS) is the world's most comprehensive and broadly adopted cloud platform, offering over 200 fully featured services from data centers globally. Millions of customers trust AWS to power their infrastructure and be more agile.\n\nThe **AWS Core Distributed Storage** engineering team designs and operates the distributed foundation behind Amazon S3, DynamoDB, and Elastic Block Store (EBS). We build the software that securely stores exabytes of data and handles hundreds of millions of requests per second.\n\n### The Role\nWe are seeking a Senior Software Development Engineer to lead the architectural evolution of our next-generation distributed storage subsystems. You will design, build, and deploy low-latency storage microservices using Go (Golang) and Rust, tackling hardware-software co-design, distributed consensus, and autonomous self-healing replication.\n\n### Key Responsibilities:\n- Design and build mission-critical distributed storage services in Go (Golang) and Rust capable of handling millions of QPS.\n- Implement Paxos and Raft consensus protocols, epoch-based replication, and distributed transaction coordinators.\n- Optimize disk I/O, NVMe SSD write amplification, and memory caches to achieve sub-millisecond p99.9 read latencies.\n- Lead the design of fault-tolerant systems that automatically detect hardware bit rot, silent data corruption, and disk failures.\n- Deploy services across AWS global infrastructure using automated CI/CD deployment pipelines with zero customer impact.\n- Drive rigorous operational excellence: monitor service health, define SLA/SLO metrics, and lead root-cause analysis for high-severity events.\n- Mentor junior engineers and participate in hiring top engineering talent across AWS.\n\n### Minimum Qualifications:\n- Bachelor\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or related technical field.\n- 5+ years of non-internship professional software development experience in Go (Golang), Rust, C++, or Java.\n- 3+ years of experience with distributed systems architecture, concurrency, consistency protocols, and low-latency systems.\n- Strong proficiency in Linux systems programming, multithreading, memory management, and performance analysis.\n- Experience with automated testing, CI/CD, and building high-availability cloud infrastructure.\n\n### Preferred Qualifications:\n- Master\u2019s or PhD in Computer Science with a focus on Distributed Systems or Storage.\n- Hands-on experience with NVMe over Fabrics (NVMe-oF), SPDK, or kernel bypass networking.\n- Demonstrated leadership in delivering large-scale distributed storage architectures.\n\n### Compensation & Benefits:\n- **Base Salary Range:** $185,000 \u2013 $265,000 USD per year.\n- **Equity:** Amazon Restricted Stock Units (RSUs) with strong multi-year vesting schedule.\n- **Benefits:** Comprehensive healthcare, 401(k) matching, fertility benefits, employee discount, and generous parental leave.",
