      company_name: 'Snowflake',
      canonical_title: 'Senior Systems Engineer, Cloud Infrastructure & Data Plane (Golang)',
      title: 'Senior Systems Engineer, Cloud Infrastructure & Data Plane (Golang)',
      description_text: "### About Snowflake Data Cloud\nSnowflake enables every organization to mobilize their data with Snowflake\u2019s Data Cloud. Customers use the Data Cloud to unite siloed data, discover and securely share data, and execute diverse analytic workloads across multiple clouds.\n\nThe **Cloud Infrastructure & Data Plane Core** group builds the distributed virtual warehouse cluster managers, secure sandbox runtimes, and low-latency storage engines that execute SQL queries over exabytes of enterprise data.\n\n### The Role\nWe are looking for a Senior Systems Engineer to join our Cloud Infrastructure team. You will design, build, and optimize high-throughput distributed microservices in Go (Golang) that orchestrate hundreds of thousands of elastic virtual compute clusters across AWS, Azure, and GCP.\n\n### Key Responsibilities:\n- Architect and scale distributed cluster management microservices in Go (Golang) capable of provisioning virtual warehouses in seconds.\n- Design multi-cloud abstraction layers and control planes spanning AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud Platform.\n- Build fault-tolerant distributed locking, health monitoring, and automated cluster recovery microservices.\n- Optimize network throughput, inter-node communication, and memory utilization for distributed query execution nodes.\n- Implement automated security sandboxes, IAM role federation, and zero-trust networking across customer execution environments.\n- Partner with database kernel engineers to profile query execution bottlenecks, disk spilling, and distributed cache hit ratios.\n- Participate in on-call rotations, maintaining 99.99% availability for enterprise Data Cloud customers.\n\n### Minimum Qualifications:\n- Bachelor\u2019s or Master\u2019s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or related technical field.\n- 5+ years of software development experience building distributed backend systems in Go (Golang), Java, or C++.\n- Proven experience with cloud-native architectures, containerization (Docker, Kubernetes), and multi-cloud infrastructure.\n- Strong foundation in distributed systems concepts: consensus, replication, partitioning, and fault tolerance.\n- Proficiency in Linux systems programming, multithreading, and performance profiling.\n\n### Preferred Qualifications:\n- Experience building multi-tenant infrastructure across AWS, Azure, and GCP.\n- Familiarity with database internals: query optimization, columnar storage formats (Parquet, ORC), and vectorization.\n- Track record of shipping high-reliability cloud services at enterprise scale.\n\n### Compensation & Benefits:\n- **Base Salary Range:** $195,000 \u2013 $275,000 USD per year.\n- **Equity:** Snowflake Restricted Stock Units (RSUs) with compelling equity package.\n- **Benefits:** 100% employer-covered health/dental/vision insurance, 401(k) with company match, flexible time off, and continuous education stipends.",
